---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import SideMark from '../../components/SideMark.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Explain — Andrew Shiau"
  description="A skill that turns something I just worked out into an explainer with a diagram and a quiz that checks it landed."
>
  <div class="grid">
    <div class="back"><a href="/">← Index</a></div>
  </div>

  <div class="grid">
    <div class="c1-10">
      <SideMark href="/work/explain/" />
      <h1>Explain</h1>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="grid">
    <p class="dek c1-8" style="margin-top:var(--unit)">
      A skill that turns something I just worked out — an incident, a system, a recipe —
      into one self-contained explainer: a diagram, and a short quiz that checks whether
      the idea landed.
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- TYPE B, beat 2: named head over the page's argument (was unheaded prose). -->
  <div class="grid sect">
    <div class="shead">
      <h2>Why the quiz</h2>
      <div class="sbody">
        <p>
          Writing something down proves I can phrase it. It doesn't tell me whether anyone
          understood it. Three questions a reader gets right does, so every explainer this
          skill writes ends in a quiz.
        </p>
        <p>
          One prompt produces both halves, in one HTML file, set in whichever house style
          suits the piece.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="grid">
    <div class="block c1-6">
      <span class="st">Both examples below are live.</span>
      <span class="sd">Answer a quiz question — correct turns red, wrong gets an ✕.</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="grid sect">
    <!-- a .links staircase follows, not a paragraph — head flush left -->
    <div class="c1-12"><h2>Explainers</h2></div>
  </div>
  <div class="grid" style="margin-top:var(--unit)">
    <div class="links">
      <a href="/writing/10x-is-a-loop/">
        10x is a loop, not a prompt <span class="arrowc">→</span>
        <span class="lu">AI-assisted engineering, from the public research</span>
      </a>
      <a href="/writing/canele/">
        What makes a canelé custardy <span class="arrowc">→</span>
        <span class="lu">one ratio, from six recipes normalized</span>
      </a>
      <a href="/writing/loops-vs-graphs/">
        Loops vs graphs <span class="arrowc">→</span>
        <span class="lu">agent architecture — when a loop should become a graph</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- TYPE B close: the facts colophon. -->
  <div class="grid sect">
    <div class="facts">
      <div class="frow">
        <div class="fm">Form</div>
        <div class="ftx">
          One prompt in, one self-contained HTML file out: the explanation, a diagram, and
          a scored quiz, set in whichever house style suits the piece.
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="frow">
        <div class="fm">The test</div>
        <div class="ftx">
          If a reader can't pass the quiz, I rewrite the explainer. It's the only check
          the skill makes.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
